---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Competition — Mausam Kumar Giri";
const description =
  "Mausam Kumar Giri in skill competitions: IndiaSkills web technologies bronze, IndiaSkills cloud computing gold, gold in Wollongong, and cloud computing for India at WorldSkills Shanghai 2026.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="page">
    <p class="kicker">West Champaran · 2024 – 2026</p>
    <h1>Competition</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Two skills. First the screen. Then a cloud built against a clock. Shanghai is the world floor. The medal that year was won earlier, in Wollongong.
    </p>

    <figure>
      <img
        src="/worldskills_mausamgiri_3.jpg"
        alt="Mausam Kumar Giri at the India station, WorldSkills Shanghai 2026"
        width="1600"
        height="1200"
      />
      <figcaption>Shanghai, September 2026.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>IndiaSkills 2024 · Web technologies · Bronze</h2>
    <p>
      West Champaran, for Bihar. The Bihar Skill Development Mission lists the bronze. That week was structure and speed on a page. It is not the skill I took to Shanghai.
    </p>
    <p class="sources">
      <a href="https://staging-skillmissionbihar.mkcl.org/world-skill/india-skill-competition-2024/timeline">Bihar Skill Development Mission</a>
    </p>

    <h2>IndiaSkills 2026 · Cloud computing · Gold</h2>
    <p>
      I changed skill. Networks, identity, automation, and recovery, graded under a clock. National gold. The people around that result include Bihar Skill Development Mission, ETHNUS, and the expert group.
    </p>

    <h2>Wollongong · June 2026 · Gold</h2>
    <p>
      The Global Skills Challenge, 23–29 June 2026, was a rehearsal of WorldSkills: sixteen countries, the same scoring system. DD News records the cloud result. Gold, Mausam Kumar Giri, Bihar. Silver, Japan. Bronze, Singapore.
    </p>
    <p class="sources">
      <a href="https://ddnews.gov.in/en/team-india-wins-5-medals-at-global-skills-challenge-australia-2026-strengthens-worldskills-shanghai-preparations/">DD News</a>
    </p>

    <h2>WorldSkills Shanghai 2026 · Cloud computing · India</h2>
    <p>
      23–26 September 2026. I was India’s competitor in cloud computing. The medals in the skill went to China, Korea, and Singapore. This is the fact of representing India.
    </p>
    <p class="sources">
      <a href="https://worldskills2026.com/skills/cloud-computing/">WorldSkills Shanghai, cloud computing</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
